            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Arises after an injury to nociceptive systems. Examples of the most common causes are polyneuropathies, acute zoster neuralgia, and postherpetic neuralgia. The differential diagnosis and management are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
